                <pb facs="0424" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/14504: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-16T20:00:00-05:00">December 16, 1938—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>422. Your 787, December 16, 3 p.m., paragraph 2. In the contingency mentioned,
                    the Department desires that you continue to maintain <pb facs="0425" n="421"
                        xml:id="pg421"/> the position of this Government as expressed to the
                    Japanese Government both in writing and orally.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
